1. TRUE POSITIVE (submitted): DefaultValidator.getValidDirectoryPath() at line 469 uses String.startsWith() without a trailing file separator for path containment check. While both dir and parent are canonicalized, the missing trailing separator creates a prefix collision bypass (e.g., /var/data2 passes a check for parent=/var/data). The secondary canonical equality check doesn't prevent this because the sibling path IS already in canonical form.

